RAW SENSOR GENERATION
Four primitive variables:

x1
x2
x3
x4.

x3 and x4:
independent noise.

x1:
standard normal
in both latent modes.

x2
has the same marginal scale
in both modes.

The useful information is:
RELATIONAL.

When:
Z=0

x2 ≈ +x1 + noise.

When:
Z=1

x2 ≈ -x1 + noise.

Therefore:

x1 alone
and
x2 alone

carry little useful context identity.

But:
their relationship
does.

GENERIC DERIVED-OBSERVABLE LIBRARY
Candidate constructions include:

x1 - x2

x1 + x2

|x1 - x2|

|x1 + x2|

x1 * x2

x1 / (|x2| + epsilon)

(x1-x2)^2

and:
a distractor product
x3*x4.

The transform names are:
generic mathematical operations.

No transform is labeled:
useful.

OBSERVABLE MODEL
Each candidate observable receives:
a small one-dimensional predictive model.

Primary confirmation used:
a linear probability diagnostic
with clipping.

Metric:
held-out Brier-score improvement.

Each derived observable also pays:
its own synthetic active-compute cost.

