DECISION
AR-H104 is POSITIVE WITH A MULTIPLE-COMPARISON / REPRESENTATION-SEARCH LIMIT.

Supported synthetically:

- raw individual variables can fail to expose a real latent context;
- generic derived observables can recover useful relational state;
- derived sensing substantially improves held-out prediction;
- independent validation strongly suppresses spurious observable birth;
- large candidate libraries create severe multiple-comparison pressure;
- representation search must be memory/evidence priced.

Not demonstrated:

- temporal derived sensors;
- nonlinear learned sensor networks;
- spatial multi-cell feature construction;
- sensor grammar inheritance;
- sensor transform retirement;
- physical sensing cost.

